# Starter habits for development builds. Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and
# put your own habits in it. Never commit real names: this repo is public.
# Format, versioning and re-applying: docs/how-to/starter-habits.md
#
# One line of JSON. "version" is a whole number; raise it to re-apply the list.
# The first apply REFUSES a database that already holds check-ins, notes or
# frozen days (your real phone data). Add "replace":true to the JSON to allow
# it once; the old habits and history are deleted. Prefer a dev-variant build
# (own bundle id, own data) so this never matters.
# Per habit:
#   name      required, up to 32 characters
#   category  required, one of the built-in categories (supplies icon and color):
#             Health, Fitness, Mindfulness, Productivity, Learning, Finance,
#             Social, Home, Creativity, Other
#   perWeek   optional, 1-7 times a week (omit for daily)
#   target    optional, {"amount": 1-999, "unit": "min"} for a counted habit
#             (omit for a simple check)
#   reminders optional, [{"hour": 8, "minute": 30, "weekdays": [1,3,5]}]
EXPO_PUBLIC_STARTER_PROFILE='{"version":1,"habits":[{"name":"Example stretch","category":"Fitness","perWeek":3},{"name":"Example reading","category":"Learning","target":{"amount":15,"unit":"min"}}]}'
